Z||000036||AusFiero||07-18-2001||02:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ferrari_momo:<BR><B>AusJim,<BR> good day mate, lol.   i will be in thailand for 3 weeks.  heard that many thai people go there to Australia to study.  <BR> yes, i'd like to get into this business deal with you.  promise me that we wont get into arguments like many business partners. lol, life is too short to worry about little things.  <BR> Peace be with you all.<BR>pat k<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>LOL no probs pat. I am not the argumentive type personally. Have fun in Thailand, I was there in 99. Lots of Aussies go there to get drunk and party on  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. Lots of thais come here to study yes. Lots of Aussies go to Thailand to study women if you get my drift. <P>Avoid Bangkok it is a smelly dirty sheethole.<BR>Coastal areas are great, can dine on Lobster for about $6 US for a whole lobster. Prawns so big it only take 3 prawns to make a kilo.<P>How to keep the prostitutes away. Hire one to sit with you when trying to have a drink in peace. <P>If in Pattaya definately go to Hollywood nightclub. Just ask any tuk tuk driver or cab, they know where it is, tourists don't. It is a locals club and man does it rock. I seen Venga Boys when I went there...FREE. It also has a laser show the likes I have never seen anywhere. I was put onto it after meeting a guy from the Aussie embassy at Hard Rock Cafe one night.<P>Also be careful which internet cafe you go too, some are real ripoffs, most aren't.<P>If you have accomodation booked, don't stay there to long, it costs about 1/3 of the cost once your in town and hotels are plentiful.<BR>||||reg||1
